{number: 141}
{title: Savior, MoreThan Life to Me}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] Savior, more than life to me,
I am [Db] clinging, clinging [Ab] close to Thee;
Let Thy precious blood applied
Keep me [Eb7] ever, ever near Thy [Ab] side.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Ab] Every day, every hour,
Let me [Db] feel Thy cleansing [Ab] pow'r;
May Thy tender love to me
Bind me [Eb7] closer, closer, Lord, to [Ab] Thee.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Through [Ab] this changing world below,
Lead me [Db] gently, gently [Ab] as I go;
Trusting Thee, I cannot stray,
I can [Eb7] never, never lose my [Ab] way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Let [Ab] me love Thee more and more,
Till this [Db] fleeting, fleeting [Ab] life is o'er;
Till my soul is lost in love,
In a [Eb7] brighter, better world a-[Ab] bove.
{end_of_verse}
